cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Decidion FoldQ: Explainable Hybrid Quantum-Classical Optimization
  for mRNA Secondary-Structure Prediction
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pahari
    given-names: Siddhartha
    email: siddhartha.pahari@mail.utoronto.ca
    affiliation: Decidion AI / University of Toronto
  - family-names: Solanki
    given-names: Jainish
    email: jainish.solanki@mail.utoronto.ca
    affiliation: Decidion AI / University of Toronto
repository-code: https://github.com/Sjainish04/decidion-foldq
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research platform that formulates RNA secondary-structure
  prediction as a Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization problem and
  solves it with classical, quantum-inspired, and gate-based quantum methods,
  validating every candidate against ViennaRNA. Its central contribution is a
  four-gate diagnostic ladder that attributes each result to candidate
  generation, the energy model, or the optimizer, rather than reporting an
  unexplained score. Built for the WISER Summer Program 2026 Moderna Challenge.
  No quantum-advantage claim is made.
keywords:
  - RNA secondary structure
  - QUBO
  - quantum optimization
  - QAOA
  - simulated annealing
  - ViennaRNA
  - pseudoknots
  - mRNA
